<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐᾰφής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁφή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>soft</i>, of seeds ready to germinate, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.17.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					1.14
				</span></i>
			; of tumours, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔεικτος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.3
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>susceptible</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.588e
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εστάτως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, σκευαζομένη ἔμπλαστρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aët.
					16.47
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>having a gentle, delicate touch</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					2.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὐαφὲς τῶν δακτύλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Im.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπόγγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paul.Aeg.
					4.21
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -έστατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			 H.: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. μετάβασις</span>
			an <i>easy, unforced</i> transition, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				55
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶς</span>, 
				Ion.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, <i>gently</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεικνύναι</span> point
			out <i>gently</i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				11.18.4
			</span></i>.</div>
